  <!-- ============ THEMES ============ -->
  <section class="section" id="themes">
    <span class="section-label">Comfort</span>
    <h2>Themes for Long Sessions</h2>
    <p>VibeCrew sessions can run for hours. A good theme reduces eye strain and makes block boundaries, errors, and highlights easier to scan.</p>

    <h3>Recommended settings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Theme:</strong> Warp Dark (default) or Dracula are good baselines. Avoid pure-black backgrounds &mdash; <code>#0a0a0b</code> to <code>#1a1a2e</code> range is easier on the eyes</li>
      <li><strong>Font size:</strong> 14&ndash;15px for comfortable reading at arm's length. Warp Settings &rarr; Appearance &rarr; Font Size</li>
      <li><strong>Sync with OS:</strong> Enable in Settings &rarr; Appearance to auto-switch between light and dark themes based on macOS appearance</li>
      <li><strong>Input position:</strong> "Bottom" (default) keeps the command line at the bottom. Some developers prefer "Top" so output scrolls downward &mdash; try both</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Custom themes</h3>
    <p>Create a YAML file in <code>~/.warp/themes/</code>. Warp also has a <strong>Theme Creator</strong> that generates a matching color palette from any background image.</p>

    <pre><code><span class="code-label">~/.warp/themes/vibecrew-dark.yaml</span>name: VibeCrew Dark
accent: '#a78bfa'
background: '#0a0a0b'
foreground: '#fafafa'
details: darker
terminal_colors:
  normal:
    black: '#27272a'
    red: '#f87171'
    green: '#4ade80'
    yellow: '#fbbf24'
    blue: '#60a5fa'
    magenta: '#a78bfa'
    cyan: '#67e8f9'
    white: '#fafafa'
  bright:
    black: '#71717a'
    red: '#fca5a5'
    green: '#86efac'
    yellow: '#fde68a'
    blue: '#93c5fd'
    magenta: '#c4b5fd'
    cyan: '#a5f3fc'
    white: '#ffffff'</code></pre>

    <p>This theme matches the VibeCrew documentation color palette. The accent color is the same purple used throughout the docs and status bar.</p>
  </section>

