  <!-- ============ WISPR FLOW ============ -->
  <section class="section" id="wispr-flow">
    <span class="section-label">Bonus Tip</span>
    <h2>Voice Input with Wispr Flow</h2>
    <p>Typing prompts is the slowest part of working with Claude Code. <strong>Wispr Flow</strong> is an AI-powered voice dictation app for macOS (and Windows/iOS) that lets you speak your prompts directly into Warp &mdash; or any text field. It's roughly <strong>4&times; faster than typing</strong> and works inside any app, including your terminal.</p>

    <h3>Why it works so well with VibeCrew</h3>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h4>Natural-language prompts</h4>
        <p>VibeCrew commands like <code>/idea "..."</code> and <code>/new-feature "..."</code> take plain English descriptions. Speaking them is faster and often produces better, more detailed prompts than typing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>Multi-tab speed</h4>
        <p>When you're juggling 3&ndash;4 Warp tabs with different Claude sessions, dictating a quick instruction is much faster than typing it out in each tab.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>Context-aware formatting</h4>
        <p>Wispr Flow automatically handles capitalization, punctuation, and formatting. Say "add a login page with email and password fields comma Google OAuth comma and a remember me checkbox" and it produces clean, punctuated text.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>Hands-free review</h4>
        <p>While Claude builds a feature in one tab, dictate your next instruction in another tab without switching your hands between keyboard and trackpad.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3>Getting started</h3>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><strong>Install Wispr Flow</strong> from the <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/wispr-flow-ai-voice-keyboard/id6497229487" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mac App Store</a> or from <a href="https://wisprflow.ai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">wisprflow.ai</a>. The free tier includes 2,000 words per week.</li>
      <li><strong>Grant accessibility permissions</strong> when prompted. Wispr Flow needs this to type into active text fields.</li>
      <li><strong>Set your hotkey.</strong> The default activation key works, but you can customize it in Wispr Flow preferences. A good choice is a key you don't use often so you can toggle dictation quickly.</li>
      <li><strong>Start speaking into Warp.</strong> Click into a Warp prompt, press your Wispr Flow hotkey, and speak your command naturally. Wispr Flow transcribes it directly into the terminal input.</li>
    </ol>

    <Callout type="tip" title="Pro tip: think out loud">
      <p>Voice input changes how you interact with Claude. Instead of condensing your thoughts into a terse typed prompt, you can think out loud: "I want to add a settings page where users can update their display name and email. It should validate the email format client-side and show a success toast when saved." The extra detail actually helps Claude produce better results on the first try &mdash; and it takes the same 5 seconds to say that it would take to type "add settings page."</p>
    </Callout>
  </section>
